{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1784303329","published":"2026-07-17T15:49:16Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:31:47.113692325Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-42012","CVE-2026-42013","CVE-2026-42015"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-42012, CVE-2026-42013, CVE-2026-42015","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: CN fallback not precluded by URI SAN\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-42012.patch: treat a URI subject\n       alternative name as precluding the fallback to Common Name\n       hostname matching, per RFC 6125 6.4.4, in\n       lib/x509/hostname-verify.c.\n     - CVE-2026-42012\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: CN/DN fallback not precluded by oversized SAN\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-42013.patch: keep the CN (hostname) and\n       DN-email fallbacks disabled when a subject alternative name is\n       oversized instead of silently ignoring it, per RFC 6125 6.4.4, in\n       lib/x509/hostname-verify.c and lib/x509/email-verify.c.\n     - CVE-2026-42013\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: PKCS#12 bag out-of-bounds write\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-42015.patch: fix an off-by-one in the\n       PKCS#12 bag element bounds check that allowed writing past the\n       32-element array, in lib/x509/pkcs12_bag.c.\n     - CVE-2026-42015","affected":[{"package":{"name":"gnutls-bin","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/gnutls-bin?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.4.10-4ubuntu1.9+tuxcare.els4"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu16.04els/CLSA-2026-1784303329.json"}},{"package":{"name":"gnutls-doc","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/gnutls-doc?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.4.10-4ubuntu1.9+tuxcare.els4"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu16.04els/CLSA-2026-1784303329.json"}},{"package":{"name":"guile-gn